    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "An Ammeter is always connected in series due to low resistance, while a Voltmeter is connected in parallel due to high resistance.",
        "In a series circuit, current remains constant; in a parallel circuit, voltage remains constant across all branches.",
        "Fuse wire is made of an alloy with a low melting point and high resistance to protect circuits from overcurrent."
